acceptance_criterion:
Create a typed adapter boundary covering:
- health/capability probe;
- workspace resolution/creation where allowed;
- document upload/index;
- document removal/retirement;
- retrieval/query;
- document/workspace lookup.

Define explicit states such as:
- available;
- unavailable;
- degraded;
- unauthorized;
- invalid response.

Persist/configure retrieval behavior including:
- top-k defaults;
- score threshold;
- deduplication;
- source-authority preference;
- allowed scopes;
- context-length limits;
- future reranking hooks.

Translate Source ownership into knowledge scope:
- global official;
- organization;
- institution;
- teacher.

When a new active source revision replaces an old one:
- create/index new binding;
- retire/detach prior active binding only after safe replacement;
- preserve historical mapping.

Persist query/audit metadata:
- query ID/hash;
- actor/tenant;
- retrieval profile version;
- workspaces queried;
- result source revisions;
- timestamps;
- warnings/errors.

Provide engineering commands to:
- probe AnythingLLM;
- index one eligible synthetic/private fixture source;
- query scoped knowledge;
- inspect provenance/binding;
- retire binding.

Synthetic/non-copyrighted fixtures covering:
- official global source;
- institution source;
- teacher source;
- scoped curriculum metadata.

Cover:
- inactive revision indexing;
- duplicate indexing;
- supersession;
- foreign-tenant workspace/result;
- unknown remote document;
- stale checksum;
- AnythingLLM timeout/401/5xx/malformed response;
- prompt-injection-like source text;
- authority misclassification;
- missing exact retrieval profile;
- excessive context size.

During implementation, run only impacted tests:
- adapter change -> adapter tests;
- indexing/lifecycle change -> knowledge indexing tests;
- retrieval/isolation change -> retrieval tests;
- migration/model change -> migration/PostgreSQL tests;
- Docker/settings change -> targeted config/container smoke.

Provide `python -m app.day7_verify` demonstrating:
- gateway fake health/probe;
- active revision indexing;
- inactive revision rejection;
- idempotent duplicate indexing;
- tenant isolation;
- exact SourceRevision provenance;
- authority separation;
- deterministic retrieval/context pack;
- unavailable gateway graceful failure;
- retrieval profile version;
- audit persistence.

At final Day 7 checkpoint only:
- targeted Day 7 suite green;
- Ruff/Mypy relevant scope green;
- migration/PostgreSQL checks green if changed;
- frontend only if changed;
- Compose only if Day 7 container/config changed;
- one full regression before merge;
- independent review has no blocker/P1/major finding, or any Founder-approved external-review exception is explicitly documented;
- evidence map D7-01…D7-36;
- D5-DS01/#16 unchanged;
- Day 8 remains LOCKED pending Founder approval.

Persist separately:
- Eduvijna stable `docSource` identity used for retrieval matching;
- AnythingLLM returned location/document identity required for retirement/de-embedding.

For real vector-search hits:
- require `metadata.docSource`;
- match it exactly against the persisted Eduvijna stable identity;
- never fall back to chunk UUID;
- never match from query/request provenance;
- missing or unknown `docSource` => reject/drop with audit-visible warning.

Repeated indexing of the same SourceRevision/checksum/profile:
- reuses the same stable identity;
- does not duplicate bindings;
- does not create a new provenance identity.

Extend `python -m app.day7_verify` with deterministic evidence that:
- stable identity is deterministic;
- exact `docSource` is persisted;
- mismatched gateway echo fails closed;
- vector hit maps through stable `docSource`;
- unknown/missing identity is rejected;
- exact SourceRevision provenance is preserved.

Before closure:
- targeted tests green;
- Ruff/Mypy relevant scope green;
- backend-only Compose Day 7 tests green;
- exact-SHA Codex review has no blocker/P1/major issue;
- no additional automatic repair after 3 iterations of this new task;
- original Day 7 PR #22 remains unmerged;
- Day 8 remains LOCKED;
- D5-DS01 / issue #16 remains unchanged.

Add deterministic fixtures for:
- one clean question first-pass approval;
- one question repaired then approved;
- small generic multi-item batch;
- curriculum-grounded and institution-scoped context;
- checkpoint resume.

Cover:
- malformed model JSON;
- author/solver disagreement;
- hallucinated provenance;
- foreign-tenant context attempt;
- blocking Day 6 validation;
- prompt-injection-like evidence;
- duplicate output;
- gateway timeout/401/5xx;
- repair exhaustion;
- interrupted/resumed run;
- idempotent replay.

At final checkpoint only:
- D8 targeted suite green;
- Ruff/Mypy changed scope green;
- checkpoint persistence/migration tests green if schema/dependency changed;
- SQLite/PostgreSQL compatibility green;
- one final full regression;
- Docker Compose smoke if dependencies/container config changed;
- manual ChatGPT code review clean under Founder workflow;
- evidence map D8-01…D8-36 complete;
- D5-DS01/#16 unchanged;
- Day 9 remains LOCKED pending Founder signoff.

Add synthetic fixtures for:
- one MCQ with distinct misconception-driven distractors;
- one item requiring one diagnostic repair;
- curriculum-grounded misconception tags;
- institution-scoped context.

Cover:
- hallucinated misconception code;
- wrong-subject/grade misconception;
- correct option mislabeled as misconception;
- duplicate misconception tags;
- ambiguous second-correct distractor;
- unsupported evidence ref;
- foreign-tenant evidence;
- prompt-injection-like source text;
- malformed model JSON;
- gateway timeout/401/5xx.

At final checkpoint only:
- D9 targeted suite green;
- Ruff/Mypy green;
- migration/SQLite/PostgreSQL compatibility green if changed;
- one final full regression;
- Docker Compose smoke if runtime/dependencies changed;
- manual ChatGPT exact-HEAD review clean;
- evidence map D9-01…D9-36 complete;
- D5-DS01/#16 unchanged;
- Day 10 remains LOCKED pending Founder signoff.
